    "b-40-quality-prompt-quality-is-a-judg-2": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-prompt-quality-is-a-judg-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Prompt quality is a judgment about the model-facing result, not merely whether\nthe source compiles. A good prompt puts material on the correct face, gives\neach section a clear job, reads in execution order, and spends tokens only on\ndistinctions that improve behavior or output."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-the-dimensions-below-mak-3": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-the-dimensions-below-mak-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The dimensions below make that judgment explicit. Scoring them is optional;\nreviewing all six is not."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-divider-4": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-divider-4",
      "type": "divider",
      "props": {},
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-evaluation-dimensions-5": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-evaluation-dimensions-5",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Evaluation Dimensions"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-token-efficiency-6": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-token-efficiency-6",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Token Efficiency"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-every-section-and-instru-7": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-every-section-and-instru-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Every section and instruction should earn its cost. Remove material that does\nnot change behavior, handling, or output, including repeated rules, ceremonial\nstages, and slots filled only because a template provides them."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-token-efficiency-is-not-8": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-token-efficiency-is-not-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Token efficiency is not brevity at any cost. A boundary or priority that\nprevents a recurring failure earns its space; a shorter paraphrase of another\nsection does not."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-structural-precision-9": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-structural-precision-9",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Structural Precision"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-the-structure-should-hel-10": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-the-structure-should-hel-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The structure should help the model parse the job. Check that tags are\nsemantic, sections follow the canonical order, workflow and rules remain\ndistinct, and any required output shape is literal rather than implied."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-structural-precision-als-11": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-structural-precision-als-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Structural precision also includes placement. Behavior belongs in the system\nprompt, reusable reference material belongs in self-describing context blocks,\nthe live picture belongs in state, and tool definitions belong to the tool\nlayer. A clean XML tree is still structurally wrong when its contents are on\nthe wrong face."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-reasoning-fit-12": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-reasoning-fit-12",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Reasoning Fit"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-reasoning-scaffolding-sh-13": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-reasoning-scaffolding-sh-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Reasoning scaffolding should match the task and its observed failure modes.\nAdd a workflow phase, critique pass, or other technique when it reduces a\nspecific risk. Remove it when it adds ceremony without improving the result."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-the-test-is-causal-an-a-14": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-the-test-is-causal-an-a-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The test is causal: an author should be able to say what failure the added\nstructure prevents. Complexity alone does not establish that it is useful."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-robustness-15": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-robustness-15",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Robustness"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-the-prompt-should-handle-16": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-the-prompt-should-handle-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The prompt should handle the difficult inputs and execution conditions that\nare plausible for its job: missing state, ambiguous requests, incomplete\nreferences, tool limits, conflicting requirements, and important edge cases."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-robustness-comes-from-ex-17": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-robustness-comes-from-ex-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Robustness comes from explicit priorities and observable conditions, not from\ntrying to enumerate every possible exception. State-navigated agents should\nrecover their position from named state fields; single-output prompts should\nsay how to treat ambiguous or malformed input when that choice affects the\nanswer."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-output-value-18": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-output-value-18",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Output Value"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-the-result-should-be-spe-19": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-the-result-should-be-spe-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The result should be specific, useful, and actionable for its consumer. A\nresponse can satisfy its format and still fail this dimension by producing\npolished generalities, unsupported claims, or details with no decision value."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-evaluate-the-actual-resu-20": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-evaluate-the-actual-resu-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Evaluate the actual result against the prompt's purpose and, where present,\ngoal and success criteria. Formatting compliance is evidence of control, not\nproof of value."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-promptkit-integrity-21": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-promptkit-integrity-21",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "PromptKit Integrity"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-the-authored-artifact-sh-22": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-the-authored-artifact-sh-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The authored artifact should preserve prompt-kit's source-of-truth and boundary\nmodel. Prompts are structured documents built from the vocabulary of the\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "canonical prompt object",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/10-canonical-prompt-object"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and quality review\nchecks that the structure is used honestly:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-declare-dynamic-values-a-23": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-declare-dynamic-values-a-23",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Declare dynamic values as variables rather than raw placeholders."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-prefer-structured-conten-24": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-prefer-structured-conten-24",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Prefer structured content to raw passthrough when the existing vocabulary already expresses the shape."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-keep-runtime-loader-sche-25": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-keep-runtime-loader-sche-25",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Keep runtime loader schemas, tool definitions, and tool implementation out of prompt sections."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-use-valid-semantic-tags-26": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-use-valid-semantic-tags-26",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Use valid semantic tags and stable, non-duplicated ids where ids are needed."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-context-blocks-are-suppl-27": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-context-blocks-are-suppl-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Context blocks are supplied outside the prompt and describe for themselves\nwhat they contain and when to consult them. Do not use a prompt-side context\ninventory to couple otherwise independent reference blocks to the system\nprompt."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-rendered-output-judgment-28": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-rendered-output-judgment-28",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Rendered-Output Judgment"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-authors-shape-rendered-x-29": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-authors-shape-rendered-x-29",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Authors shape rendered XML-tagged Markdown through the prompt document; the\nrenderer only expresses those choices. Review the final model-facing text\nbecause a valid document can still produce a prompt that reads poorly."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-semantic-tags-30": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-semantic-tags-30",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Semantic Tags"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-use-tags-whose-names-exp-31": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-use-tags-whose-names-exp-31",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Use tags whose names explain the section's role, such as "
        },
        {
          "insert": "<purpose>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ",\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "<state_structure>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "<workflow>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", or "
        },
        {
          "insert": "<quality_bar>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Avoid generic names such\nas "
        },
        {
          "insert": "<section_1>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "<notes>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "<misc>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". If a reader cannot predict what a\nsection carries from its tag, the boundary is not doing useful semantic work."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-tags-delineate-regions-32": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-tags-delineate-regions-32",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Tags delineate regions; they do not replace prose. Inside workflow fields,\nuse ordinary sentences and lists instead of inventing tags for every branch,\ncondition, or task."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-linear-reading-order-33": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-linear-reading-order-33",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Linear Reading Order"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-rendered-prompts-should-34": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-rendered-prompts-should-34",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Rendered prompts should read from top to bottom without forward references.\nAgent prompts use this order, omitting only sections documented as optional:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-xml-35": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-xml-35",
      "type": "code",
      "props": {
        "language": "xml"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "<purpose>\n<goal>\n<state_structure>\n<workflow>\n<error_handling>\n<success_criteria>\n<rules>"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-rules-is-last-so-the-36": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-rules-is-last-so-the-36",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "<rules>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is last so the non-negotiables are recent when the model acts. There\nis no "
        },
        {
          "insert": "<tools>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " section, context inventory, or "
        },
        {
          "insert": "<reminders>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " section. Tools are\nattached by the runtime, context blocks describe themselves, and reminders are\nreplaced by a small trailing rules section."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-single-output-prompts-us-37": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-single-output-prompts-us-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Single-output prompts use this order:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-xml-38": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-xml-38",
      "type": "code",
      "props": {
        "language": "xml"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "<purpose>\n<instructions>\n<workflow>       <!-- staged prompts only -->\n<output_format>\n<constraints>"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-constraints-is-last-39": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-constraints-is-last-39",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "<constraints>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is last for the same recency reason. Examples are not a prompt\nsection; when they are necessary, they arrive as a self-describing context\nblock."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-runtime-data-boundaries-40": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-runtime-data-boundaries-40",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Runtime Data Boundaries"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-do-not-interleave-live-d-41": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-do-not-interleave-live-d-41",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Do not interleave live data with standing instructions. Dynamic state is\nrendered as the separate live picture whose fields are declared in\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "<state_structure>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Reference packets remain separate context blocks, and\ntool schemas remain in the tool layer."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-this-separation-makes-au-42": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-this-separation-makes-au-42",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "This separation makes authority and freshness visible. A current document,\ntool result, or user-provided payload can contain imperative-looking text; its\nplacement should still make clear that it is data to evaluate rather than a\nstanding instruction to obey."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-output-formats-and-lists-43": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-output-formats-and-lists-43",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Output Formats and Lists"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-where-a-single-output-pr-44": {
      "id": "b-40-quality-where-a-single-output-pr-44",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Where a single-output prompt requires a response shape, show its literal\nskeleton in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "<output_format>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". A schema, fenced structure, or fixed field list\nlets the model copy the form instead of inferring it from prose."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-quality-use-numbered-lists-only-45": {
